{"t": 145.381, "n": 113, "ev": "result", "ok": true, "text": "Phase 1 is built. `tests/test_usage_limit.py`, `tests/test_run.py` and `tests/test_council_run.py` pass together (51 tests, run with `-n 0`). I wrote the tests first, and they failed for the right reason: the refused step was rerun three times. I didn't run the full suite, lint or mypy.\n\n- **Rows 1.1 to 1.5:** all five are marked with `✓ 2026-11-26`, and the plan's status is now `in-progress`.\n- **`nodes.py`:** `_session` stops its infra loop at once on a refused session, and every `agent_run` record now carries `usage_limit` and `usage_limit_resets_at`. `step` records escalation cause `usage_limit` with `infra_spent` false and the reset instant.\n- **`council_run.py`:** a refused member or chair sets the new `limited` field and is not read as a missing answer. `finish` writes the attempt with `escalate` `usage_limit` and no artifacts.\n- **Blocked command:** my first attempt to mark the plan used `sed`, and the harness denied it. I made the same edits with the Edit tool.\n\nI checked the specs outside the plan's front matter for anything this phase makes false, and found none.\n\nARTIFACT phase_note: Ran tests/test_usage_limit.py, tests/test_run.py and tests/test_council_run.py (all pass, -n 0). Deviations: (1) row 1.3 asks that ok member sessions are not rerun on the rerun, but that needs resume and open_run (rows 4.6, 4.8, phase 4), so test 1.3 covers refused member and refused chair only; the rerun clause is for phase 4. (2) In council_run.py I also made `dispatch` and `tally_now` return early when `limited` is set, so no later round, tally or chair runs after a refusal; small extra beyond the row text, in the row's own file. (3) The refused member re-ask is read the same way as a refused first session. Specs checked outside the plan's front matter: none made false.", "subtype": "success", "is_error": false, "session_id": "33389494-a1d2-47d3-a89f-7df2b43c3085"}
